      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "83c5dfcf-b259-5a4e-a383-859b2dfdf6ff",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The point $(\\frac{9\\pi }{2},1)$ is on the graph.\n- **II.** $x=-4\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote.\n- **III.** $x=\\frac{-6\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "deb93c83-eeb9-5717-a480-9412c0acf661",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "92d51cf7-0069-5372-b9ec-e39642247322",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8ea88387-67ae-5e42-99be-8fa90247ee46",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "8ea88387-67ae-5e42-99be-8fa90247ee46"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "333d3ae6-616f-560c-9a73-d8fa1a4a5671",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "5091bdef-300f-5946-8cf1-e00712a5aac1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "64667f23-cd64-599c-8859-10e751423d5a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "64667f23-cd64-599c-8859-10e751423d5a"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "56dd08e7-9a6d-59b4-a65a-4910ec642677",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "2e7c950a-8437-5595-9e01-05ed99c899a6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "df6b9c68-0de2-5581-b6ab-b11021294e83",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "2e7c950a-8437-5595-9e01-05ed99c899a6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement I is true.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{-6\\pi }{2}$ is an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement III is false.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
