    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cc8e9fe1-85ac-5c6e-a8fa-c1f558946f5d",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The point $(\\frac{7\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph.\n- **II.** $x=-15\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote.\n- **III.** $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bbaa7619-a1d2-52b4-b960-72abd4a093ce",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "3e84f48b-3725-5eeb-bbaf-fb8add370990",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d4285137-1b5d-5db0-bcc5-98a7ab01dda2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "d4285137-1b5d-5db0-bcc5-98a7ab01dda2"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fcf4bb56-fa2b-5f81-8c42-27ad46bf237c",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "8b7beaab-4299-5235-b21c-b7b076b4c10d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "14f5a8be-a5c6-539f-a88a-5a5fca1f2436",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "14f5a8be-a5c6-539f-a88a-5a5fca1f2436"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "24abcf34-316a-53ca-82df-4c0c4ffd2c52",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "a112b8f3-6cc3-5ab8-86f3-b3b1740da4f8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6a625c67-ec7b-5738-9ee7-f90da7afe55c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "6a625c67-ec7b-5738-9ee7-f90da7afe55c"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $-1$ at $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement I is true.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{13\\pi }{2}$ is not an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
